For t\\gtrsim 10^{3} yr, the neutron star interior has relaxed thermally (Nomoto & Tsuruta 1981), we can use the flux-to-core-temperature relation for several values of B including B=0 to derive the relationship between T_{\\rm eff} and the cooling time. The technique is straightforward during the epoch of neutrino cooling. However, since photon emission is enhanced, the epoch of photon cooling will begin slightly earlier, and the time dependence of the temperature will have a slightly different slope. For the neutrino cooling model, we use the modified URCA process (_e.g._ Shapiro & Teukolsky 1983)

